-- title:
--   Fixed ring of a node automorphism is a crossing model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (the algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$ as implemented in Mathlib), a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}:A\to k$.
--
--   *Moduli data.* An element $a\in k$ is assumed to lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no non-zero affine point killed by $q$, and $a=0$ or $a=1728$; consequently `jWidth a`, defined as $3$ if $a=0$, as $2$ if $a=1728$ and as $1$ otherwise, equals $3$ or $2$. An element $l\in k$ satisfies $l^{q^2}=l$, $l\neq 0$, $16l\neq 1$ and the Legendre relation $a\cdot\bigl((16l)^2(16l-1)^2\bigr)=256\bigl((16l)^2-16l+1\bigr)^3$.
--
--   *Coefficient ring.* $K$ is a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_0:=$ `coeffSubring A K` is the intersection $A\cap K$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with reduction $\mathrm{red}_0:=$ `redRestrict red K`$\colon A_0\to k$ obtained from $\mathrm{red}$ by restriction. It is assumed that $y\in A_0$ reduces to $l$, that $\varpi\in A_0$ generates the kernel of $\mathrm{red}_0$ in the sense that $\mathrm{red}_0 c=0$ if and only if $c=\varpi d$ for some $d\in A_0$, and that $q=\varpi^{e_K}\varepsilon$ in $A_0$ with $e_K\ge 1$ and $\varepsilon$ a unit.
--
--   *The node ring.* $S:=$ `lambdaLocalizedAtPoint q A₀ red₀ l (l^q)` is the subring of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ with `pointEval` $s\neq 0$ — that is, the value of $s$ at $(X_0,X_1)=(l,l^q)$ after applying $\mathrm{red}_0$ to the coefficients is non-zero — and $f\cdot\mathrm{ev}(s)=\mathrm{ev}(r)$, where $\mathrm{ev}=$ `lambdaEval q A₀` is the evaluation sending $X_0$ to the Laurent series `lambdaModC` of the modular $\lambda$-function, $X_1$ to its $q$-fold expansion `lambdaNModC`, and a coefficient to the corresponding constant Laurent series. Thus $S$ is the local ring of the $\lambda$-cover at the point $(l,l^q)$. It is assumed Noetherian and local, and $\hat S$ denotes its `maximalIdeal`-adic completion.
--
--   *The automorphism.* $g$ is a ring automorphism of $S$ subject to: `hgC`, $g$ fixes $\mathrm{ev}(C\,o)$ for every $o\in A_0$; and `hge`, the `jWidth a`-fold iterate of $g$ is the identity. Elements $\zeta_0,\zeta_0'\in A_0$ are given with $\mathrm{red}_0(\zeta_0)^{\,\mathrm{jWidth}\,a}=1$, with $\mathrm{red}_0(\zeta_0)^m\neq 1$ for $0<m<\mathrm{jWidth}\,a$, and with $\mathrm{red}_0(\zeta_0)\cdot\mathrm{red}_0(\zeta_0')=1$. Writing $H:=\mathrm{ev}(X_0-X_1^{\,q})$ and $G:=\mathrm{ev}(X_1-X_0^{\,q})$, and $\mathfrak n$ for the ideal of $S$ spanned by $\mathrm{ev}(C\,\varpi)$, $\mathrm{ev}(X_0-C\,y)$ and $\mathrm{ev}(X_1-C\,y^q)$, the two tangency hypotheses read
--   $$g(H)-\mathrm{ev}(C\,\zeta_0)\cdot H\in \mathfrak n^2+(q),\qquad g(G)-\mathrm{ev}(C\,\zeta_0')\cdot G\in \mathfrak n^2+(q),$$
--   where $(q)$ is the ideal of $S$ generated by the image of the natural number $q$ and the sum is the supremum of the two ideals.
--
--   *The completed automorphism.* $\hat g$ is a ring automorphism of $\hat S$ which is induced by $g$ levelwise: for every $n$, every $x\in\hat S$ and every $z\in S$ whose class in $S/\mathfrak m^n$ is the $n$-th component `AdicCompletion.evalₐ` of $x$, the $n$-th component of $\hat g(x)$ is the class of $g(z)$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* Put $W:=A_0[[T]]/(T-\varpi)$, i.e. the quotient of `PowerSeries A₀` by the ideal generated by $X-C\,\varpi$, and let $\bar\varpi\in W$ be the class of $C\,\varpi$. For $\pi\in W$, `UVCrossingModel W π` is the quotient of `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W` by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1-C\,\pi$, that is, the ring of formal power series in two variables over $W$ in which the product of the two variables is identified with $\pi$; it carries distinguished elements `UVCrossingModel.U`, `UVCrossingModel.V`, whose product is `UVCrossingModel.const π π`, and constants `UVCrossingModel.const`. Then there exist a ring homomorphism
--   $$\Phi:\ \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\bigl(W,\ \bar\varpi^{\,\mathrm{jWidth}\,a\cdot e_K}\bigr)\longrightarrow \hat S$$
--   and units $w,w'$ of $\hat S$ such that:
--
--   1. $\Phi$ is injective;
--
--   2. for every $z\in\hat S$, $z$ lies in the range of $\Phi$ if and only if $\hat g(z)=z$;
--
--   3. for every $o\in A_0$, $\Phi$ maps the constant `UVCrossingModel.const` attached to the class of $C\,o$ in $W$ to the image of $\mathrm{ev}(C\,o)\in S$ under the structure map $S\to\hat S$;
--
--   4. $\Phi(\mathrm{U})=w\cdot\bigl(\text{image of }G\text{ in }\hat S\bigr)^{\mathrm{jWidth}\,a}$, where $G=\mathrm{ev}(X_1-X_0^{\,q})$;
--
--   5. $\Phi(\mathrm{V})=w'\cdot\bigl(\text{image of }H\text{ in }\hat S\bigr)^{\mathrm{jWidth}\,a}$, where $H=\mathrm{ev}(X_0-X_1^{\,q})$.
--
--   So the $\hat g$-fixed subring of $\hat S$ is exactly the image of the crossing model with parameter $\bar\varpi^{\,\mathrm{jWidth}\,a\cdot e_K}$, the two coordinates going to unit multiples of the $\mathrm{jWidth}(a)$-th powers of $G$ and $H$; the exponent on $\bar\varpi$ is $\mathrm{jWidth}(a)$ times the one occurring in the branch-adapted chart $\hat S\cong\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}(W,\bar\varpi^{\,e_K})$ of [`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_uvCrossingModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_uvCrossingModel).
--
--   This is the quotient step in the analysis of a supersingular node over $j\in\{0,1728\}$, read on the Legendre ($\lambda$-level two) cover: the fixed ring of the stabiliser acting on the regular crossing with parameter $\bar\varpi^{e_K}$ is the wider crossing with parameter $\bar\varpi^{\,e\cdot e_K}$, where $e=\mathrm{jWidth}(a)$, in the spirit of Deligne–Rapoport VI.6.9 and the Mazur–Rapoport appendix. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_modularLocalizedAtPoint_uvCrossingModel_of_eq_zero_or_eq_1728`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_modularLocalizedAtPoint_uvCrossingModel_of_eq_zero_or_eq_1728) to identify the completed local ring of the modular curve at such a node.
